{
  "about": "A verbatim subset of NIST CAVP's SP 800-135 IKEv2 KDF vectors (ikev2.rsp inside ikev2.zip), plus the RFC 5903 section 8.1 ECP-256 example. Field meanings are ASKDFVS section 6.3: SKEYSEED = prf(Ni | Nr, g^ir) and DKM = prf+(SKEYSEED, Ni | Nr | SPIi | SPIr) (RFC 7296 section 2.14); DKM(Child SA) = prf+(SK_d, Ni | Nr) and DKM(Child SA D-H) = prf+(SK_d, g^ir (new) | Ni | Nr) (section 2.17); SKEYSEED(Rekey) = prf(SK_d, g^ir (new) | Ni | Nr) (section 2.18); SK_d is the first PRF-output-length octets of DKM. Lengths in 'section' are BITS, as the .rsp states them. Consumed by web/src/lib/netkeys/ikev2.ts; see references/net-key-schedules.md.",
